response_text:
## C++ Function

```cpp
#include <map>

std::pair<int, int> maxPair(const std::map<int, int>& m) {
    std::pair<int, int> maxP = *m.begin();
    for (const auto& p : m)
        if (p.second > maxP.second)
            maxP = p;
    return maxP;
}
```

## Explanation (Hindi mein)

- **Line 1:** `<map>` header include kiya
- **Function signature:** Ek `map<int, int>` leta hai aur `pair<int, int>` return karta hai
- **`maxP`:** Pehle pair ko initial maximum maan liya
- **Loop:** Har pair ko check karte hain
- **Condition:** Agar current pair ki `second` value `maxP` ki `second` se badi hai, to `maxP` update karo
- **Return:** Sabse bada pair return karte hain

## Generic Version (kisi bhi type ke liye)

```cpp
#include <map>

template<typename K, typename V>
std::pair<K, V> maxPair(const std::map<K, V>& m) {
    std::pair<K, V> maxP = *m.begin();
    for (const auto& p : m)
        if (p.second > maxP.second) maxP = p;
    return maxP;
}
```

**Note:** Empty map ke case mein `m.begin()` undefined behavior dega, isliye real code mein ek empty check bhi add kar sakte ho:

```cpp
if (m.empty()) return {};
```

# Valheim Skill Threshold Mod Banane Ka Guide

Chalo step-by-step samajhte hain ki yeh mod kaise banega.

## 1. Setup (Pehle Yeh Install Karo)

```
1. BepInEx for Valheim (mod loader)
2. Visual Studio (C# ke liye)
3. .NET Framework 4.6.1+
4. HarmonyX (patching ke liye)
```

**References add karo** apne project mein:
- `assembly_valheim.dll`
- `BepInEx.dll`
- `0Harmony.dll`

(Yeh files Valheim install folder aur BepInEx folder mein milti hain)

## 2. Logic Samajh Lo

Aapko milestones (10, 20, 30... 85) chahiye:

- Agar skill level **10** cross kare → threshold = 10
- Agar skill level **20** cross kare → threshold = 20
- ... yeh chalta rahe **85** tak
- Death pe skill level **threshold se neeche nahi** jaana chahiye

## 3. Main Mod Code

```csharp
using BepInEx;
using HarmonyLib;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using UnityEngine;

[BepInPlugin("com.yourname.skillthreshold", "Skill Threshold Mod", "1.0.0")]
public class SkillThresholdMod : BaseUnityPlugin
{
    // Har skill ka threshold yahan store hoga
    public static Dictionary<Skills.SkillType, float> Thresholds 
        = new Dictionary<Skills.SkillType, float>();

    private void Awake()
    {
        Harmony harmony = new Harmony("com.yourname.skillthreshold");
        harmony.PatchAll();
        Logger.LogInfo("Skill Threshold Mod loaded!");
    }

    // Milestone calculate karne ka function (10, 20, 30... 85)
    public static float GetThreshold(float currentLevel)
    {
        if (currentLevel < 10) return 0;

        // Har 10 ka milestone, max 85 tak
        float milestone = Mathf.Floor(currentLevel / 10f) * 10f;
        return Mathf.Min(milestone, 85f);
    }
}
```

## 4. Threshold Update Karna (Jab Level Up Ho)

```csharp
// Skill level badhne pe threshold update karo
[HarmonyPatch(typeof(Skills.Skill), "Raise")]
public static class Patch_SkillRaise
{
    public static void Postfix(Skills.Skill __instance)
    {
        var skillType = __instance.m_info.m_skill;
        float newThreshold = SkillThresholdMod.GetThreshold(__instance.m_level);

        // Agar naya threshold purane se zyada hai, to update karo
        if (!SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds.ContainsKey(skillType) || 
            SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds[skillType] < newThreshold)
        {
            SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds[skillType] = newThreshold;
        }
    }
}
```

## 5. Death Pe Skill Loss Limit Karna

```csharp
// Death pe skills lower karne wala function patch karo
[HarmonyPatch(typeof(Skills), "LowerAllSkills")]
public static class Patch_LowerAllSkills
{
    // Original method chalne se pehle thresholds yaad rakho
    public static void Prefix(Skills __instance, 
        out Dictionary<Skills.SkillType, float> __state)
    {
        __state = new Dictionary<Skills.SkillType, float>();
        foreach (var skill in __instance.m_skillData)
        {
            __state[skill.Key] = skill.Value.m_level;
        }
    }

    // Original method ke baad threshold enforce karo
    public static void Postfix(Skills __instance, 
        Dictionary<Skills.SkillType, float> __state)
    {
        foreach (var skill in __instance.m_skillData)
        {
            var skillType = skill.Key;

            if (SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds.TryGetValue(skillType, out float threshold))
            {
                // Agar level threshold se neeche gaya, to wapas threshold pe set karo
                if (skill.Value.m_level < threshold)
                {
                    skill.Value.m_level = threshold;
                    // Accumulator reset karo taaki XP sahi rahe
                    skill.Value.m_accumulator = 0f;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

## 6. Thresholds Ko Save/Load Karna (Important!)

Game band hone pe thresholds save honi chahiye, warna lost ho jaayengi:

```csharp
using System.IO;
using System.Text;

public static class ThresholdSaver
{
    private static string SavePath = 
        Path.Combine(BepInEx.Paths.ConfigPath, "skill_thresholds.txt");

    public static void Save()
    {
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        foreach (var kvp in SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds)
        {
            sb.AppendLine($"{kvp.Key}={kvp.Value}");
        }
        File.WriteAllText(SavePath, sb.ToString());
    }

    public static void Load()
    {
        if (!File.Exists(SavePath)) return;

        SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds.Clear();
        foreach (var line in File.ReadAllLines(SavePath))
        {
            var parts = line.Split('=');
            if (parts.Length == 2 && 
                System.Enum.TryParse(parts[0], out Skills.SkillType type))
            {
                SkillThresholdMod.Thresholds[type] = float.Parse(parts[1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Phir `Awake()` mein `ThresholdSaver.Load();` add karo aur game save hone pe `Save()` call karo.

## 7. Build & Test

```
1. Project ko DLL mein compile karo
2. DLL ko: Valheim/BepInEx/plugins/ folder mein daalo
3. Game start karo
4. Test: Skill level 10+ karo, phir maro,
   check karo ki level 10 se neeche nahi gaya
```

## ⚠️ Zaroori Notes

- **Method names check karlo**: Valheim updates ke baad method names (`LowerAllSkills`, `Raise`) change ho sakte hain. **dnSpy** ya **ILSpy** se `assembly_valheim.dll` decompile karke verify karo.
- **Multiplayer**: Server-client sync ke liye extra code chahiye hoga.
- **Backup**: Pehle apna world backup le lo testing ke time.

## Threshold Logic Customize Karna

Agar tum chahte ho ki milestones different ho:

```csharp
public static float GetThreshold(float currentLevel)
{
    float[] milestones = { 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80, 85 };
    float result = 0;

    foreach (float m in milestones)
    {
        if (currentLevel >= m) result = m;
    }
    return result;
}
```

---

Kya tumhe **multiplayer support** ya **per-skill config** (alag-alag skills ke liye alag rules) bhi chahiye? Batao to main woh part bhi add kar deta hoon!

# Object-Oriented Programming Principles

OOP ke teen main pillars software development ko kaafi behtar banate hain. Chaliye ek-ek karke samajhte hain.

---

## 1. Encapsulation (Data Hiding)

**Kya hai?** Data aur methods ko ek unit mein bundle karna, aur internal details ko hide karna.

**Fayde:**
- Data ki security badhti hai
- Code maintainable rehta hai
- Internal implementation change kar sakte ho bina baaki code todre

### Java Example:
```java
public class BankAccount {
    private double balance;  // private = hidden

    public void deposit(double amount) {
        if (amount > 0) balance += amount;
    }

    public double getBalance() {  // controlled access
        return balance;
    }
}
```

### Python Example:
```python
class BankAccount:
    def __init__(self):
        self.__balance = 0  # __ se private

    def deposit(self, amount):
        if amount > 0:
            self.__balance += amount

    def get_balance(self):
        return self.__balance
```

### C++ Example:
```cpp
class BankAccount {
private:
    double balance;
public:
    void deposit(double amount) {
        if (amount > 0) balance += amount;
    }
    double getBalance() { return balance; }
};
```

**Real-world:** Bank account ka balance directly modify nahi kar sakte — sirf deposit/withdraw methods se hi.

---

## 2. Inheritance (Code Reusability)

**Kya hai?** Ek class doosri class ki properties aur methods inherit kar sakti hai.

**Fayde:**
- Code reuse hota hai (DRY principle)
- Hierarchical relationships banti hain
- Maintenance easy hota hai

### Java Example:
```java
class Vehicle {
    void start() { System.out.println("Engine started"); }
}

class Car extends Vehicle {
    void openRoof() { System.out.println("Roof opened"); }
}
// Car ke paas start() bhi hai aur openRoof() bhi
```

### Python Example:
```python
class Vehicle:
    def start(self):
        print("Engine started")

class Car(Vehicle):
    def open_roof(self):
        print("Roof opened")
```

### C++ Example:
```cpp
class Vehicle {
public:
    void start() { cout << "Engine started"; }
};

class Car : public Vehicle {
public:
    void openRoof() { cout << "Roof opened"; }
};
```

**Real-world:** `Employee` → `Manager`, `Developer` — sab employees mein common attributes (name, salary) hote hain.

---

## 3. Polymorphism (Many Forms)

**Kya hai?** Same interface, alag-alag behavior. "Ek naam, kai roop."

**Do types:**
- **Compile-time** (Method Overloading)
- **Runtime** (Method Overriding)

### Java Example:
```java
class Animal {
    void sound() { System.out.println("Some sound"); }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
    void sound() { System.out.println("Bark"); }  // override
}

class Cat extends Animal {
    void sound() { System.out.println("Meow"); }
}

// Runtime polymorphism
Animal a = new Dog();
a.sound();  // Output: Bark
```

### Python Example:
```python
class Animal:
    def sound(self):
        print("Some sound")

class Dog(Animal):
    def sound(self):
        print("Bark")

# Duck typing - Python ka special feature
for animal in [Dog(), Cat()]:
    animal.sound()
```

### C++ Example:
```cpp
class Animal {
public:
    virtual void sound() { cout << "Some sound"; }
};

class Dog : public Animal {
public:
    void sound() override { cout << "Bark"; }
};
// virtual keyword runtime polymorphism enable karta hai
```

**Real-world:** Payment system — `CreditCard`, `UPI`, `Wallet` sab ka `pay()` method same call hota hai par alag kaam karta hai.

---

## Language-wise Comparison

| Feature | Java | Python | C++ |
|---------|------|--------|-----|
| Encapsulation | Strict (`private`) | Convention based (`__`) | Strict (`private`) |
| Multiple Inheritance | Nahi (interfaces se) | Haan | Haan |
| Polymorphism | `@Override` | Duck typing | `virtual` keyword |
| Access Control | Strong | Weak (naming) | Strong |

---

## Overall Benefits

✅ **Modularity** — Code chote independent parts mein divide hota hai
✅ **Reusability** — Likha hua code dobara use hota hai
✅ **Maintainability** — Bugs fix karna easy
✅ **Scalability** — Bade projects manage karna aasaan
✅ **Real-world modeling** — Asli duniya ke objects ko code mein represent karna

Koi specific principle ya language par aur detail chahiye to bataiye! 🚀

prompt_text:
Maine ek certain website se rental data lene ke liye kuch code likha hai, yahan following javascript code hai.
```javascript
const axios = require('axios');
const cheerio = require('cheerio');

const getData = async () => {
  const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1');
  const $ = cheerio.load(response.data);

  const properties = [];

  $('.listing-result').each((i, el) => {
    const property = {};

    property.title = $(el)
      .find('.property-title')
      .text()
      .trim();
    property.address = $(el)
      .find('.property-address')
      .text()
      .trim();
    property.price = $(el)
      .find('.priceText')
      .text()
      .trim();

    properties.push(property);
  });

  return properties;
};

getData().then((properties) => {
  console.log(properties);
});
```
Following error kyun aata hai?
"AxiosError: Request failed with status code 429"

response_text:
# Error 429 ka matlab

**HTTP 429 = "Too Many Requests"** — Iska matlab hai ki server aapko **rate limit** kar raha hai. Aap (ya aapka IP) bahut zyada requests bhej rahe ho, ya server ne aapko ek **bot/scraper** ke roop mein detect kar liya hai aur block kar raha hai.

## Iske main reasons:

1. **Bot detection** — realestate.com.au jaise badi websites mein strong anti-scraping protection hota hai (Cloudflare, etc.). Aapka request browser jaisa nahi lag raha, isliye block ho gaya.

2. **No User-Agent** — Axios by default ek generic User-Agent bhejta hai jo easily bot ke roop mein pehchaana jaata hai.

3. **Too many requests** — Agar aapne baar-baar code chalaya toh server ne temporarily block kar diya.

---

## ⚠️ Important Legal/Ethical Note

Pehle ye check karo:

- **`robots.txt`** — `https://www.realestate.com.au/robots.txt` dekho. Zyaadatar real estate sites scraping ko **explicitly disallow** karti hain.
- **Terms of Service** — In sites ke ToS aksar automated scraping ko **prohibit** karte hain. Violation karne par legal issues aur permanent IP ban ho sakta hai.

**Behtar approach:** Dekho ki kya site ek **official API** provide karti hai (ya RapidAPI jaisi services par third-party APIs available hain).

---

## Technical fixes (agar scraping allowed ho)

### 1. Proper headers add karo
```javascript
const response = await axios.get(url, {
  headers: {
    'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/120.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',
    'Accept': 'text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8',
    'Accept-Language': 'en-US,en;q=0.9',
  }
});
```

### 2. Requests ke beech delay daalo
```javascript
const delay = (ms) => new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
await delay(3000); // 3 second wait
```

### 3. Retry with backoff (429 ke liye)
```javascript
const getDataWithRetry = async (url, retries = 3) => {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return await axios.get(url, { headers: { 'User-Agent': '...' } });
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.response?.status === 429 && i < retries - 1) {
        const wait = Math.pow(2, i) * 2000; // exponential backoff
        console.log(`429 mila, ${wait}ms wait kar rahe hain...`);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait));
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
};
```

---

## Lekin sach yeh hai...

Cloudflare-protected sites (jaise realestate.com.au) mein sirf headers add karne se shayad kaam **nahi** karega, kyunki ye JavaScript challenges run karti hain. Agar bilkul scrape karna zaroori ho toh:

- **Puppeteer** ya **Playwright** (real browser automate karte hain) zyada effective hote hain.

**Meri salah:** Pehle official API ya legal data source dhoondho — yeh sabse safe aur reliable rasta hai. Kya aap mujhe bata sakte ho ki aap is data ko kis purpose ke liye use karna chahte ho? Main accordingly behtar suggestion de sakta hoon.

# Merge Sort: Detailed Explanation

Namaste! Chaliye is topic ko ache se samajhte hain.

## Merge Sort Kaise Kaam Karta Hai?

Merge sort **"Divide and Conquer"** strategy par based hai. Iska basic idea ye hai:

### Teen Main Steps:

1. **Divide (Baant-na):** Array ko baar-baar do halves mein todte rahte hain jab tak har piece mein sirf ek element na bach jaye (kyunki single element hamesha "sorted" hota hai).

2. **Conquer (Sort karna):** Chote pieces ko sort karte hain.

3. **Merge (Jodna):** Sorted pieces ko wapas ek sorted array mein combine karte hain.

### Visual Example:

```
        [38, 27, 43, 3, 9, 82, 10]
               /            \
      [38, 27, 43]        [3, 9, 82, 10]
        /     \              /      \
    [38]   [27,43]        [3,9]   [82,10]
            /  \           /  \    /   \
         [27] [43]       [3] [9] [82] [10]

  Ab merge karte hue upar wapas jaate hain (sorted):
         [27,43]        [3,9]   [10,82]
      [27,38,43]        [3,9,10,82]
        [3, 9, 10, 27, 38, 43, 82]  ✅
```

---

## Bubble Sort vs Merge Sort

| Feature | Bubble Sort | Merge Sort |
|---------|-------------|------------|
| **Time Complexity (Worst)** | O(n²) | O(n log n) |
| **Time Complexity (Best)** | O(n) | O(n log n) |
| **Space Complexity** | O(1) | O(n) |
| **Large data ke liye** | Bahut slow ❌ | Efficient ✅ |
| **Stable** | Haan | Haan |

### Merge Sort ke Benefits:

1. **Speed:** Bade datasets pe Merge Sort kaafi tezz hai. Maan lijiye 1 million elements hain:
   - Bubble Sort: ~10¹² operations
   - Merge Sort: ~2×10⁷ operations (lakhon guna fast!)

2. **Predictable Performance:** Merge sort hamesha O(n log n) hi rehta hai, chahe data kaisa bhi ho. Bubble sort worst case mein bahut slow ho jaata hai.

3. **Large Data ke liye Ideal:** External sorting (jab data RAM mein fit nahi hota) ke liye merge sort use hota hai.

**Trade-off:** Merge sort extra memory use karta hai (O(n)), jabki bubble sort sirf O(1) space leta hai.

---

## Rust Implementation

```rust
fn merge_sort(arr: &[i32]) -> Vec<i32> {
    // Base case: agar array mein 1 ya 0 element hai, to wo already sorted hai
    if arr.len() <= 1 {
        return arr.to_vec();
    }

    // DIVIDE: Array ko beech se do halves mein baanto
    let mid = arr.len() / 2;
    let left = merge_sort(&arr[..mid]);   // Left half ko recursively sort karo
    let right = merge_sort(&arr[mid..]);  // Right half ko recursively sort karo

    // MERGE: Dono sorted halves ko combine karo
    merge(&left, &right)
}

fn merge(left: &[i32], right: &[i32]) -> Vec<i32> {
    let mut result = Vec::with_capacity(left.len() + right.len());
    let mut i = 0; // left ka pointer
    let mut j = 0; // right ka pointer

    // Dono arrays ko compare karte hue chote element ko pehle daalo
    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] <= right[j] {
            result.push(left[i]);
            i += 1;
        } else {
            result.push(right[j]);
            j += 1;
        }
    }

    // Bache hue elements ko add karo (ek array khatam ho gaya hoga)
    result.extend_from_slice(&left[i..]);
    result.extend_from_slice(&right[j..]);

    result
}

fn main() {
    let numbers = vec![38, 27, 43, 3, 9, 82, 10];
    println!("Original array: {:?}", numbers);

    let sorted = merge_sort(&numbers);
    println!("Sorted array:   {:?}", sorted);
}
```

### Output:
```
Original array: [38, 27, 43, 3, 9, 82, 10]
Sorted array:   [3, 9, 10, 27, 38, 43, 82]
```

---

## Code ka Flow Samjhiye:

1. `merge_sort` recursively array ko todta hai (Divide).
2. Base case pe single elements milte hain.
3. `merge` function do sorted slices ko compare karke ek bada sorted array banata hai.
4. Ye process upar tak chalti hai jab tak pura array sorted na ho jaye.

---

**Practice Tip:** Mein recommend karunga ki aap ek chota array (jaise `[5, 2, 8, 1]`) lekar pen-paper pe har step trace karein. Isse recursion aur merge logic dono crystal clear ho jayenge!

Koi doubt ho to bezijhak puchiye! 😊
